# Grid A — S3D Config trace, schema-level absence (no sibling fallback)
#
# Targets: config_trace scenario + ReqConfigMapping + ShapeExplanation
# under conditions where the LLM CANNOT find a useful sibling key. Pins
# the 2026-05+ scope-axis migration: when no per-line sibling cite is
# available, the answer surface depends on the LLM emitting schema-
# level evidence (scope=file for layer-canonical files, scope=negative
# for the absence proof, scope=crossfile for "no CLI flag for this
# group" attestation).
#
# The phantom key `explore_xyz_phantom_unique_budget` is intentionally
# distinctive enough that no real key will sibling-match it: there is
# no `explore_xyz_*` family in either codrax.yaml or RuntimeSettings,
# so the LLM can't escape into a sibling-line cite. It MUST either
# (a) emit schema-level evidence to anchor the absence + the layers
# structurally, or (b) leave the answer surface thin (one-layer prose
# only — fails the multi-anchor expectation).
#
# Ground truth: explore_* group is yaml-only (no CLI override flag),
# the canonical config layer is codrax.yaml, the default-struct layer
# is internal/types/config.go (DefaultExploreHeuristics), and the
# phantom key does not exist in any layer.
#
# Eval gate: EXPECT_CONTAINS / EXPECT_NOT_CONTAINS / EXPECT_SECTIONS
# verify the answer surfaces all three layers AND mentions the
# absence explicitly. The answer doesn't need to LITERALLY say
# "scope=file" — it needs to ground each layer with a citable anchor
# (which is what schema-level scopes structurally enable).
ID="s3d"
NAME="config trace — phantom-key precedence with schema-level absence"
QUESTION="explore_xyz_phantom_unique_budget 在三层覆盖（默认值 / codrax.yaml / CLI flag）里各自的有效值是什么？给我每一层的来源锚点。"
# Required tokens (any case): codrax.yaml as a layer anchor + the
# default-struct function name + at least one absence-acknowledgement.
# 2026-05-08 broaden (LLM jitter): the case author chose
# `DefaultExploreHeuristics` as THE default-struct anchor, but a
# phantom key "explore_xyz_phantom_unique_BUDGET" actually has the
# stronger semantic kinship to `ExploreBudget` (suffix matches the
# struct name). Both functions are real production symbols
# (DefaultExploreHeuristics in internal/types/config.go:943;
# ExploreBudget in internal/types/explore_budget.go:30). The model
# answering with ExploreBudget is semantically defensible (often
# more so than the case-author's pick). Accept either.
EXPECT_CONTAINS="codrax.yaml"
# 2026-05-04 strictness audit: phantom key absence must be
# explicit. Previous bar relied on EXPECT_SECTIONS (3 layer names)
# but didn't gate on absence verdict — answer could list 3 layers
# with hallucinated values for each layer and PASS. Add EMR
# requiring an absence-acknowledgement keyword (not found / 未定义
# / does not exist / 不存在) — proves the LLM verified absence.
# 2026-05-08 jitter relax (historical PASS rate 2/6 = 33%): the
# previous bar required literal `cmd/root.go` substring (in
# EXPECT_SECTIONS). For an absence-only answer the LLM legitimately
# has nothing concrete to anchor in cmd/root.go and tends to address
# the CLI layer conceptually ("如果存在对应的 CLI flag …" / "CLI 层")
# rather than naming the entry file. The semantic "CLI layer was
# considered" is what the case actually wants to verify. Accept
# either: literal `cmd/root.go` (precise anchor), `CLI flag` /
# `CLI 层` / `flag layer` / `--<name> flag` (semantic CLI-layer
# acknowledgement). Concrete-value hallucination is still gated by
# the absence-acknowledgement clause on line 1 (claiming 默认值 = N
# contradicts 不存在 / not found).
EXPECT_MATCHES_REGEX="(not found|does not exist|未定义|不存在|absent|no such|undefined|not.*declared)
(cmd/root\.go|CLI flag|CLI 层|flag layer|--[a-z-]+ flag)
(DefaultExploreHeuristics|ExploreBudget|ExploreHeuristics|默认.*(struct|结构|配置)|default.*(struct|config|heuristic))"
# EXPECT_NOT_CONTAINS would token-split on whitespace, banning the
# question subject itself — left empty intentionally. The "must not
# hallucinate concrete numerical defaults" anti-pattern is covered
# by the absence-acknowledgement requirement above (an answer that
# claims 默认值是 N implicitly contradicts 不存在 / not found).
EXPECT_NOT_CONTAINS=""
# Two layer-name tokens MUST all appear as literal substrings,
# proving the answer didn't collapse to one layer. The CLI-layer
# anchor moved to EXPECT_MATCHES_REGEX line 2 (alternation accepting
# semantic mention) — the explore_* family is yaml-only so there is
# no specific CLI flag to point at when the key is absent.
# 2026-05-08: literal section anchor narrowed to codrax.yaml only;
# the default-struct anchor moved into EXPECT_MATCHES_REGEX above
# so it accepts either DefaultExploreHeuristics or ExploreBudget
# (or any default-struct semantic phrase).
EXPECT_SECTIONS="codrax.yaml"
